From 2f74d5f321dab853d4517e84a2e8153c5955e51a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:29:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] remote-signer: enable server codegen, add localhost E2E
 signing test, and document trust boundary

### Motivation

- Provide an end-to-end regression that exercises the real `SignerService` wire contract so tests run against the same protobuf/tonic bindings the production client uses.
- Ensure the build produces server bindings so local-only tests can mount a plaintext gRPC signer and verify signing/verification behavior.
- Capture the security analysis and reproducible vectors for the remote-signer trust boundary in a checked-in document.

### Description

- Enable generation of server bindings in the proto build pipeline by changing `tonic_build::configure().build_server(false)` to `.build_server(true)` and add a comment explaining the rationale in `crates/remote-signer/build.rs`.
- Add `tokio-stream` to workspace `Cargo.toml` and to `crates/remote-signer` dev-dependencies and update `Cargo.lock` accordingly so the test can serve gRPC with a `TcpListener` stream.
- Add a local-only `SignerService` test implementation and an async test `localhost_signer_accepts_and_verifies_conflicting_canonical_votes` in `crates/remote-signer/src/provider.rs` that starts a plaintext SignerService on localhost, uses the production gRPC client (`RemoteSigningProvider`) to sign two conflicting precommits and a proposal, and verifies the signatures with the production verifier.
- Add `docs/security/remote-signer-trust-boundary.md` containing a detailed call-chain analysis, reproducible canonical vectors, and reproduction instructions.

### Testing

- Ran `cargo test -p arc-remote-signer -- --nocapture` which executed the new `tokio::test` E2E test along with existing unit tests and they completed successfully.
- The build step that generates protobuf bindings was exercised by the tests and succeeded (server and client stubs generated without errors).
